<title>MEXICO: Penoles plans to hike chemical volumes.</title>
<headline>Penoles plans to hike chemical volumes.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Industrias Penoles, the world's largest refined silver producer, outlined plans to increase volumes of non-metals output to the year 2000 from 1996.</p>
<p>Below is a table of the increases in output volumes in its industrial chemicals and refractories division, figures in percentages.</p>
<p>		   Chemical			2000</p>
<p>		   Sodium Sulfate		  12</p>
<p>		   Magnesium Oxide		 16</p>
<p>		   Ammonium Sulphate	     57</p>
<p>Penoles said the above outlook table does not include or consider potential acquisitions, development of new businesses nor prospects under exploration.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7287902))</p>
